IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`

-- scja3-s73-touts.l4: section 73 (list of touts).
-- Layer 1, written from the text alone (SCJA1969.txt lines 4321-4371).
-- The section is about the Registrar's list and what it means for a person named, or sought to be named, in it.
-- Decision functions answer MAYBE BOOLEAN under the rule of 2026-10-29; the "until" bar of subsection (3) is encoded as the bar (ruling (d) of 2026-11-05) and again as a trace of the Registrar's duty.

§ `Section 73: list of touts`

-- src:4330 | 73.—(1) The Registrar may publish a list of persons proved to the
-- src:4331 | Registrar’s satisfaction, by evidence of general repute or otherwise, to
-- src:4332 | act as touts or unauthorised advisers to suitors or other persons having
-- src:4333 | business with or before any officer of the Supreme Court, and may
-- src:4334 | alter and amend such list.
@ref s 73(1) (src:4330-4334)
GIVEN `the person is proved to the Registrar's satisfaction, by evidence of general repute or otherwise, to act as a tout or unauthorised adviser to suitors or other persons having business with or before an officer of the Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73(1) the Registrar may include the person in the list of touts` MEANS
    IF `the person is proved to the Registrar's satisfaction, by evidence of general repute or otherwise, to act as a tout or unauthorised adviser to suitors or other persons having business with or before an officer of the Supreme Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the list is of "persons proved to the Registrar's satisfaction ... to act as touts or unauthorised advisers", and the subsection says nothing of a person not so proved
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4342 | (3) A person’s name must not be included in the list until the person
-- src:4343 | has been heard or had an opportunity of being heard against such
-- src:4344 | inclusion.
@ref s 73(3) (src:4342-4344)
-- Ruling (d) of 2026-11-05: an "until" bar is encoded as the bar.  JUST TRUE: the name cannot yet be included.  JUST FALSE: the person has been heard, or has had the opportunity.
GIVEN `the person has been heard against the inclusion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has had an opportunity of being heard against the inclusion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73(3) the person's name cannot yet be included in the list` MEANS
    IF `the person has been heard against the inclusion` OR `the person has had an opportunity of being heard against the inclusion`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be included in the list until the person has been heard or had an opportunity of being heard"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:4336 | (2) The Registrar may, by general or special order, exclude from the
-- src:4337 | precincts of the Supreme Court any person whose name is included in
-- src:4338 | the list, except when that person is a party to or a witness in any
-- src:4339 | proceedings in the Supreme Court, when that person is to be allowed
-- src:4340 | to remain for such time as is necessary.
@ref s 73(2) (the power) (src:4336-4340)
GIVEN `the person's name is included in the list` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a party to or a witness in proceedings in the Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73(2) the Registrar may exclude the person from the precincts of the Supreme Court` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person's name is included in the list`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is over "any person whose name is included in the list"
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the person is a party to or a witness in proceedings in the Supreme Court`
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except when that person is a party to or a witness in any proceedings in the Supreme Court"
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:4336 | (2) The Registrar may, by general or special order, exclude from the
-- src:4337 | precincts of the Supreme Court any person whose name is included in
-- src:4338 | the list, except when that person is a party to or a witness in any
-- src:4339 | proceedings in the Supreme Court, when that person is to be allowed
-- src:4340 | to remain for such time as is necessary.
@ref s 73(2) (the exception) (src:4336-4340)
GIVEN `the person's name is included in the list` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a party to or a witness in proceedings in the Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73(2) the person is to be allowed to remain in the precincts for such time as is necessary` MEANS
    IF `the person's name is included in the list` AND `the person is a party to or a witness in proceedings in the Supreme Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the allowance is for "that person" when "a party to or a witness in any proceedings", and the text says nothing of anyone else
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4346 | (4) An appeal lies to a Judge sitting in chambers in the General
-- src:4347 | Division from an order made by the Registrar to include a person’s
-- src:4348 | name in the list.
@ref s 73(4) (src:4346-4348)
GIVEN `the order was made by the Registrar to include the person's name in the list` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73(4) an appeal lies to a Judge sitting in chambers in the General Division` MEANS
    IF `the order was made by the Registrar to include the person's name in the list`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the appeal lies "from an order made by the Registrar to include a person's name in the list", and the text says nothing of any other order
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4357 | (5) The decision of the Judge sitting in chambers in the General
-- src:4358 | Division is final.
@ref s 73(5) (src:4357-4358)
GIVEN `the decision is the decision of the Judge sitting in chambers in the General Division on an appeal under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73(5) a further appeal lies from the decision` MEANS
    IF `the decision is the decision of the Judge sitting in chambers in the General Division on an appeal under subsection (4)`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The decision of the Judge sitting in chambers in the General Division is final."
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of the decision of the Judge sitting in chambers in the General Division only
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4362 | (6) A copy of the list must be kept hung up in the Registry and must
-- src:4363 | be published in the Gazette.
@ref s 73(6) (src:4362-4363)
-- The duty is the Registrar's; for the person it means that the list is not secret.
GIVEN `the Registrar has published a list of touts under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73(6) a copy of the list must be kept hung up in the Registry and published in the Gazette` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has published a list of touts under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says what is to be done with "the list" and says nothing of a time when there is no list
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4365 | (7) A person whose name appears in the list of touts under
-- src:4366 | section 39 of the Family Justice Act 2014, or the list of touts under
-- src:4367 | section 62 of the State Courts Act 1970, is deemed to be included in
-- src:4368 | the list under this section, and vice versa.
@ref s 73(7) (into this list) (src:4365-4368)
GIVEN `the person's name appears in the list of touts under section 39 of the Family Justice Act 2014` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's name appears in the list of touts under section 62 of the State Courts Act 1970` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73(7) the person is deemed to be included in the list under this section` MEANS
    IF `the person's name appears in the list of touts under section 39 of the Family Justice Act 2014`
       OR `the person's name appears in the list of touts under section 62 of the State Courts Act 1970`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deeming is of "a person whose name appears in" one of the two other lists
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4365 | (7) A person whose name appears in the list of touts under
-- src:4366 | section 39 of the Family Justice Act 2014, or the list of touts under
-- src:4367 | section 62 of the State Courts Act 1970, is deemed to be included in
-- src:4368 | the list under this section, and vice versa.
@ref s 73(7) (vice versa) (src:4365-4368)
GIVEN `the person's name appears in the list under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73(7) the person is deemed to be included in the lists under section 39 of the Family Justice Act 2014 and section 62 of the State Courts Act 1970` MEANS
    IF `the person's name appears in the list under this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "and vice versa" runs only from the list under this section to the two other lists
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The regulative twin of subsection (3): the Registrar shall not include the person's name in the list until the person has been heard or had the opportunity.
-- Time is in abstract units; the number is the time at which the person is heard, or has the opportunity.
DECLARE `s 73(3) party` IS ONE OF
    `s 73(3) the Registrar`

DECLARE `s 73(3) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 73(3) includes the person's name in the list`

-- src:4342 | (3) A person’s name must not be included in the list until the person
-- src:4343 | has been heard or had an opportunity of being heard against such
-- src:4344 | inclusion.
@ref s 73(3) (the Registrar's duty) (src:4342-4344)
GIVEN `the time at which the person has been heard or has had an opportunity of being heard` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 73(3) party` `s 73(3) act`
`s 73(3) the Registrar must not include the person's name in the list until the person has been heard` MEANS
    PARTY `s 73(3) the Registrar`
    SHANT `s 73(3) includes the person's name in the list`
    WITHIN `the time at which the person has been heard or has had an opportunity of being heard`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "s 73(3): a person's name must not be included in the list until the person has been heard or had an opportunity of being heard against such inclusion"
